NOTE ON THE DATA

This licence covers the code in this repository. It does not cover, and does
not need to cover, the data the code compiles:

* FAA NASR 28-Day Subscription -- a work of the United States Government, in
  the public domain. No licence, royalty, or attribution is required.
* OurAirports -- the publisher's own wording is "All data is released to the
  Public Domain, and comes with no guarantee of accuracy or fitness for use."
  That is a dedication, not a named instrument; this file does not restate it
  as CC0, because naming a specific licence would assert a stronger and more
  specific grant than the one OurAirports actually made. Attribution is
  appreciated but not required.

  OurAirports aggregates from further sources -- it credits the discontinued
  NGA DAFIF, community sites, and individual contributors -- and does not
  state those sources' own copyright status. So the worldwide layer rests on
  the publisher's dedication rather than on a chain this project can verify.
  Users in jurisdictions that recognise database rights distinct from
  copyright (e.g. EU Directive 96/9/EC) should make their own assessment. The
  `source` column on every row records which layer it came from, so a consumer
  who needs only the US Government layer can filter to source = 'nasr'.

The compiled database is therefore public-domain data and carries no
attribution or copyleft obligation. It is NOT certified for navigation.
